Dialogue: 0,00:00:08.30,00:00:11.01,Default,,0,0,0,,In the first world war, and for the \Nfirst time, in the history of man,
Dialogue: 0,00:00:11.05,00:00:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,nations combined to fight against nations, \Nusing the crude weapons of those days.
Dialogue: 0,00:00:16.97,00:00:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The second world war \Ninvolved every continent on the globe,
Dialogue: 0,00:00:20.14,00:00:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and men turned to science \Nfor new devices of warfare,
Dialogue: 0,00:00:23.52,00:00:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,which reached an unparalleled peak \Nin their capacity for destruction.
Dialogue: 0,00:00:27.53,00:00:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, fought with the terrible \Nweapons of super science,
Dialogue: 0,00:00:31.45,00:00:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,menacing all mankind and every creature \Non earth, comes...
Dialogue: 0,00:00:36.37,00:00:42.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The war of the worlds
Dialogue: 0,00:01:42.98,00:01:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,No one would have believed \Nin the middle of the 20th century,
Dialogue: 0,00:01:45.65,00:01:49.27,Default,,0,0,0,,that human affairs \Nwere being watched keenly and closely
Dialogue: 0,00:01:49.36,00:01:52.53,Default,,0,0,0,,by intelligences greater than man's.
Dialogue: 0,00:01:52.61,00:01:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet., across the Gulf of space, \Non the planet, Mars,
Dialogue: 0,00:01:56.57,00:01:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,intellects vast and cool and unsympathetic
Dialogue: 0,00:01:59.74,00:02:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,regarded our earth with envious eyes,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:02.83,00:02:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,slowly and surely, \Ndrawing their plans against us.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:07.46,00:02:12.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Mars is more than 140 million miles \Nfrom the sun,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:12.09,00:02:15.97,Default,,0,0,0,,and for centuries, it has been \Nin the last stages of exhaustion.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:16.09,00:02:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,At night, temperatures \Ndrop far below zero,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:20.14,00:02:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,even at its equator.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:22.27,00:02:24.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The inhabitants of this dying planet
Dialogue: 0,00:02:24.52,00:02:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,looked across space \Nwith instruments and intelligences
Dialogue: 0,00:02:27.23,00:02:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,of which we have scarcely dreamed,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:30.07,00:02:34.15,Default,,0,0,0,,searching for another world \Nto which they could migrate.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:34.32,00:02:38.28,Default,,0,0,0,,They could not go to pluto, \Noutermost of all the planets,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:38.37,00:02:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,and so cold, that its atmosphere \Nlies frozen on its surface.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:44.12,00:02:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,They couldn't go to Neptune or uranus,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:46.54,00:02:50.42,Default,,0,0,0,,twin worlds in eternal night \Nand perpetual cold,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:50.50,00:02:53.21,Default,,0,0,0,,both surrounded by \Nan unbreathable atmosphere
Dialogue: 0,00:02:53.30,00:02:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,of methane gas and ammonia vapor.
Dialogue: 0,00:02:57.26,00:02:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,The martians considered saturn,
Dialogue: 0,00:02:59.55,00:03:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,an attractive world with its many moons \Nand beautiful rings of cosmic dust,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:04.68,00:03:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,but its temperature is close \Nto 270 degrees below zero,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:10.40,00:03:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,and ice lies 15,000 miles \Ndeep on its surface.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:15.11,00:03:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Their nearest world was giant Jupiter,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:17.70,00:03:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,where there are Titanic cliffs \Nof lava and ice,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:20.70,00:03:23.37,Default,,0,0,0,,with hydrogen flaming at the tops,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:23.45,00:03:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,where the atmospheric pressure \Nis terrible,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:25.08,00:03:29.12,Default,,0,0,0,,thousands of pounds to the square inch.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:29.21,00:03:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,They couldn't go there.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:31.04,00:03:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Nor could they go to Mercury, \Nnearest planet to the sun.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:34.50,00:03:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,It has no air,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:36.30,00:03:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,and the temperature at its equator \Nis that of molten lead.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:41.14,00:03:42.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Of all the worlds,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:42.76,00:03:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,that the intelligences on Mars \Ncould see and study,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:47.23,00:03:49.77,Default,,0,0,0,,only our own warm earth
Dialogue: 0,00:03:49.90,00:03:53.65,Default,,0,0,0,,was green with vegetation, \Nbright with water,
Dialogue: 0,00:03:53.73,00:03:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,and possessed a cloudy atmosphere \Neloquent of fertility.
Dialogue: 0,00:03:59.36,00:04:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It did not occur to mankind that \Na swift fate might be hanging over us,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:04.37,00:04:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,or that from the blackness of outer space,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:07.16,00:04:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,we were being scrutinized and studied,
Dialogue: 0,00:04:10.79,00:04:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,until at the time of our nearest approach
Dialogue: 0,00:04:13.75,00:04:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,to the orbit of Mars, \Nduring a pleasant summer season...
Dialogue: 0,00:04:30.10,00:04:33.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is that a fireball, or something? \N- Boy, that's big!
Dialogue: 0,00:04:33.15,00:04:34.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's a comet.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:38.15,00:04:39.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, that had me scared.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:39.28,00:04:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder where it lit.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:40.49,00:04:42.45,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miles away, I bet you. \N- Hey, let's go find it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:04:42.49,00:04:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That probably dropped halfway to pomona.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:44.07,00:04:46.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- It was nearer than that. \N- I'm gonna see. Who's coming?
Dialogue: 0,00:04:48.08,00:04:52.54,Default,,0,0,0,,- This is pine summit. I got a smoke. \N- 160, 30.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:52.67,00:04:56.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Azimuth reading: 160 degrees, 30 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,00:04:56.71,00:05:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Big? I'll bet it's as big as anything \Nthat ever lit in California.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:01.51,00:05:04.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You better get something over there. \NIt's started a Blaze already.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:10.81,00:05:13.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Over here. Hey, let's go this way.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:13.35,00:05:14.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You there, with the shovel!
Dialogue: 0,00:05:27.87,00:05:29.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me get in there!
Dialogue: 0,00:05:29.62,00:05:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Out of the way! Out of the way!
Dialogue: 0,00:05:34.33,00:05:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring that hose over here!
Dialogue: 0,00:05:36.46,00:05:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,We're getting it licked, fellas. \NKeep at it.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:39.13,00:05:40.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, grab this.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:41.05,00:05:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Joe, Joe, lend a hand over here.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:44.76,00:05:47.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Number three to d.O. Number three to d.O.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:48.22,00:05:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,D.o. To number three, come in.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:50.02,00:05:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,We're getting this under control. \NWe won't need any more help. Over.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:53.52,00:05:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay. Send the tanker in,
Dialogue: 0,00:05:54.98,00:05:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,but you can stand by \Nuntil that thing cools off. Over.
Dialogue: 0,00:05:58.73,00:06:01.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I think somebody ought \Nto check on it. Over.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:01.11,00:06:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, there's some fellows \Nfishing at pine summit.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:03.32,00:06:04.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I think they're scientists.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:04.91,00:06:08.99,Default,,0,0,0,,They probably saw it come down. \NI'll let 'em know. What's it look like?
Dialogue: 0,00:06:09.45,00:06:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't get near enough \Nto see it very well. It's too hot.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:13.08,00:06:14.96,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's a whale of a size.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:23.38,00:06:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I got a message for you.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:26.26,00:06:28.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the guys \Nfrom pacific tech, ain't you?
Dialogue: 0,00:06:28.22,00:06:29.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:30.64,00:06:32.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like the fishing was good.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:32.47,00:06:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Have some?
Dialogue: 0,00:06:38.94,00:06:40.82,Default,,0,0,0,,It's about that meteor.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:42.32,00:06:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,They say it's a whopper.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:46.82,00:06:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The district officer phoned us \Nat the lookout up on the summit.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:49.95,00:06:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you might be interested.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:51.95,00:06:54.16,Default,,0,0,0,,It's about 10 or 12 miles from here, \Nover by Linda Rosa.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:54.25,00:06:56.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Are they sure it's a meteor? \NIt didn't come down like one.
Dialogue: 0,00:06:56.96,00:06:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. \NCame down in kind of spurts, didn't it?
Dialogue: 0,00:07:01.80,00:07:05.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you fellas will have \Nto figure it out. You're scientists.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:05.09,00:07:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,All I know is, they say it's as big \Nas a house, and practically red-hot.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:08.72,00:07:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to borrow your car \Nand take a look at it in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:11.43,00:07:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We ought to get back.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:12.60,00:07:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- I can fly bilderbeck down in your plane. \N- Okay.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:15.43,00:07:17.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The insurance is paid up.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:17.48,00:07:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Light? \N- No, I'll smoke it later.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:36.12,00:07:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did you watch it come down? \N- I seen it from my window.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:42.38,00:07:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Harold. Harold. Look here a minute.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:45.17,00:07:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Step over to your left. \NJust a little and hold it.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:48.18,00:07:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Smile.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:49.34,00:07:52.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It must've hit way up there, \Nand then skidded along the gully.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:52.72,00:07:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,After it stopped, all that loose earth \Nand stuff shook down over it.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:56.02,00:07:58.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- Excuse me. \N- I guess most of it's buried.
Dialogue: 0,00:07:58.56,00:08:00.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That's 12 feet thick, easy. Maybe more.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:00.77,00:08:02.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Meteors always run heavy.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:02.56,00:08:06.28,Default,,0,0,0,,They won't be able to haul this one \Naway to no museum.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:06.61,00:08:09.20,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll be a real good attraction \Nfor Sunday drivers.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:09.70,00:08:13.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Better than a lion farm, or a snake pit. \NWe won't have to feed it.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:13.45,00:08:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure. We can sell the tamales, \Nand the enchiladas, and the hot dogs, too!
Dialogue: 0,00:08:16.62,00:08:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah! Ice cream, cold drinks, souvenirs.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:18.62,00:08:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we should put up \Na few picnic tables.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:21.08,00:08:23.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no. Then they'd bring \Ntheir own lunches.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:24.92,00:08:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the idea, buck?
Dialogue: 0,00:08:26.59,00:08:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- Gonna dig for gold? \N- You think you're kidding?
Dialogue: 0,00:08:29.59,00:08:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gonna be like having a gold mine \Nin our own backyard.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:34.18,00:08:36.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna get a closer look at it.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:42.31,00:08:44.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Reckon it's solid all through?
Dialogue: 0,00:08:44.69,00:08:47.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Lucky it didn't come down \Nin the middle of town!
Dialogue: 0,00:08:47.44,00:08:50.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder who owns this property.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:51.15,00:08:52.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it, over there.
Dialogue: 0,00:08:52.36,00:08:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are you gonna do... \N- Feels pretty darn hot!
Dialogue: 0,00:08:55.87,00:08:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the idea of the shovel?
Dialogue: 0,00:08:57.66,00:08:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,- Be careful, buck. \N- Yeah, watch it, buck.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:02.67,00:09:03.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's pretty hot there.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:06.50,00:09:09.55,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did you see it come down? \N- Yes. I was fishing up in the hills.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:09.63,00:09:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you must've caught \Nplenty with all that tackle.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:11.72,00:09:15.01,Default,,0,0,0,,There were three of us. \NThe others flew back in my plane.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:16.26,00:09:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand why a meteor that size \Ndidn't make a bigger crater.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:19.60,00:09:21.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It hit sideways, and skidded in.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:21.73,00:09:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,At least that's what I think. \NI don't really know.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:24.52,00:09:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,But the ranger said a scientist \Nis coming from pacific tech.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:27.15,00:09:28.23,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll tell us.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:28.36,00:09:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Clayton forrester. Ever hear of him?
Dialogue: 0,00:09:30.44,00:09:32.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that fellow \Ntrying to do over there, dig it out?
Dialogue: 0,00:09:32.86,00:09:36.70,Default,,0,0,0,,He's top man in astro and nuclear physics. \NHe knows all about meteors.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:38.20,00:09:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You seem to know all about him.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:39.95,00:09:44.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I did a thesis on modern scientists, \Nworking for my master's degree.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:44.29,00:09:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did it do you any good? \N- Why, sure. I got it.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:49.80,00:09:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Say, do you have a match? \N- No, I'm sorry. I don't smoke.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:54.05,00:09:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Forrester's the man \Nbehind the new atomic engines.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:56.64,00:09:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,They had him on the cover of time.
Dialogue: 0,00:09:58.35,00:10:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, you've got to rate to get that.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:00.77,00:10:02.10,Default,,0,0,0,,He isn't that good.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:02.39,00:10:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now, how can you \Nsay that when you don't even know him?
Dialogue: 0,00:10:04.73,00:10:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I do know him. Slightly.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:07.23,00:10:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's he like? \N- Well, he's like...
Dialogue: 0,00:10:11.03,00:10:12.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Like...
Dialogue: 0,00:10:16.91,00:10:20.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you certainly don't look like \Nyourself in that getup, Dr. forrester,
Dialogue: 0,00:10:20.33,00:10:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm happy to meet you, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:22.33,00:10:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Sylvia Van buren. \NI teach library science over at usc.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:25.67,00:10:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't know how to stop you.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:27.42,00:10:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I might have \Nrecognized you without the beard,
Dialogue: 0,00:10:29.75,00:10:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and you didn't wear glasses \Non the time cover.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:32.01,00:10:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,They're really for long distance.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:33.38,00:10:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,When I want to look at something close, \NI take them off.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:52.53,00:10:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, you could fry eggs on that thing!
Dialogue: 0,00:10:55.07,00:10:57.74,Default,,0,0,0,,All that sand will keep the heat in \Nfor a long time.
Dialogue: 0,00:10:57.82,00:11:00.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Uncle Matthew, \Nthis is Dr. Clayton forrester.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:00.62,00:11:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,My uncle, Dr. Matthew Collins, \Npastor of the community church.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:03.70,00:11:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, I... how do you do, Dr. forrester? \N- How do you do, sir?
Dialogue: 0,00:11:07.54,00:11:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,00:11:16.34,00:11:19.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What you got in here, fella? \NTicking like a bomb.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:22.76,00:11:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a geiger counter \Nfor detecting radioactivity.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:26.35,00:11:29.90,Default,,0,0,0,,We did a little bit of surveying \Nwhile we were up in the hills.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:40.41,00:11:41.57,Default,,0,0,0,,It's that meteor.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:42.53,00:11:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It's radioactive?
Dialogue: 0,00:11:43.83,00:11:47.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. Difficult to account \Nfor a reaction like that.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:52.71,00:11:54.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at this thing. It's going crazy.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:54.96,00:11:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe we ought to keep people \Naway from it, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:11:57.05,00:11:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Might be a good idea.
Dialogue: 0,00:11:58.59,00:11:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll post two or three deputies.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:00.05,00:12:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,They can make sure \Nit doesn't start any more fires, too.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:03.05,00:12:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, that meteor's either very light,
Dialogue: 0,00:12:05.10,00:12:07.93,Default,,0,0,0,,which is unheard of, \Nor else it's hollow somehow.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:08.48,00:12:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,If it were heavy and solid,
Dialogue: 0,00:12:09.98,00:12:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,it would have made \Na tremendous crater when it landed.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:13.86,00:12:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I'll wait around \Nuntil it cools off.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:16.99,00:12:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,If you tell me of a place in town, \NI'd like to clean up.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:20.28,00:12:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd be delighted if you'd stay \Nat my house, Dr. forrester.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:22.99,00:12:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:24.66,00:12:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably won't be cool \Nfor another 24 hours.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:27.04,00:12:29.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What do people do around here \Non a Saturday?
Dialogue: 0,00:12:30.08,00:12:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They don't do much of anything.
Dialogue: 0,00:12:31.58,00:12:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a square dance \Nat the social hall this evening.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:07.08,00:13:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, let's take another look at it.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:36.23,00:13:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Almost cold now, ain't it?
Dialogue: 0,00:13:37.82,00:13:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It won't start any more fires. \NWe might as well go home.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:40.53,00:13:42.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, no sense staying out here.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:42.95,00:13:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,00:13:49.83,00:13:52.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! It's moving!
Dialogue: 0,00:14:10.31,00:14:12.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a bomb.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:12.18,00:14:14.19,Default,,0,0,0,,It don't go off last night.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:14.27,00:14:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's gonna go off now, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:14:16.15,00:14:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It's an enemy sneak attack.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:18.19,00:14:21.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let's get out of here. \N- Wait a minute. Wait a minute.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:22.94,00:14:26.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Bombs don't unscrew.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:26.36,00:14:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,It's no meteor, that's for sure.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:31.16,00:14:34.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Darnedest thing I ever saw.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:34.50,00:14:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The way that's unscrewing.
Dialogue: 0,00:14:44.97,00:14:47.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Dr. forrester. You having fun?
Dialogue: 0,00:14:47.30,00:14:50.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep. And you want to know \Nwhat I was thinking?
Dialogue: 0,00:14:50.51,00:14:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,If we could gather all the energy \Nexpended in just one square dance,
Dialogue: 0,00:14:53.73,00:14:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,we could send that meteor \Nback to where it came from.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:44.48,00:15:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,- Must be somebody in there. \N- Who?
Dialogue: 0,00:15:47.70,00:15:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where do you think they come from? \N- How would I know?
Dialogue: 0,00:15:50.03,00:15:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I read someplace \NMars is near the earth right now.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:53.70,00:15:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Happens every 18, 20 years, they say.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:57.12,00:15:59.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Men from Mars.
Dialogue: 0,00:15:58.08,00:16:01.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:01.58,00:16:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe these are not men, not like us.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:04.80,00:16:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything human \Ndoesn't have to look like you and me.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:12.55,00:16:16.72,Default,,0,0,0,,If it's men from Mars, \Nwe ought to let them know we're friendly.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:16.81,00:16:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't fool around with something \Nwhen you don't know what it is.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:19.81,00:16:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,We'd be the first to make \Ncontact with them, see?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:22.56,00:16:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,We'd be in all the papers.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:24.82,00:16:26.11,Default,,0,0,0,,How about that?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:26.19,00:16:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,We could show them we're friendly, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:27.69,00:16:29.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Walk out there with a white flag.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:30.45,00:16:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, I got an old sugar sack in my car.
Dialogue: 0,00:16:42.33,00:16:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,What are we going to say to them?
Dialogue: 0,00:16:46.71,00:16:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,"Welcome to California.”
Dialogue: 0,00:16:49.72,00:16:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:22.29,00:17:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We're friends! Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:26.13,00:17:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, there! Open up!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:28.42,00:17:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- How they gonna understand us? \N- We'll talk in sign language.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:32.18,00:17:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- They'll understand us, all right. \N- Sure. Sure!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:36.72,00:17:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody understands \Nwhen you wave the white flag,
Dialogue: 0,00:17:38.89,00:17:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,you wanna be friends.
Dialogue: 0,00:17:40.56,00:17:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, there! Open up!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:42.81,00:17:44.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on out! We're friends!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:44.65,00:17:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right! We welcome you!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:47.57,00:17:49.23,Default,,0,0,0,,We're friends! Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,00:17:54.36,00:17:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey! Hey! \N- Hey! Hey!
Dialogue: 0,00:18:02.87,00:18:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the fuse box?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:04.79,00:18:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No smooching in the dark, folks.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:09.30,00:18:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Any candles around?
Dialogue: 0,00:18:10.84,00:18:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, look! Look! \NAll the lights in town have gone out!
Dialogue: 0,00:18:17.93,00:18:20.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Somebody's found some candles.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:20.64,00:18:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Zippy? \N- T like it in the dark.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:22.27,00:18:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Call the electric company \Nand see what happened.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:23.85,00:18:25.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:35.91,00:18:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey! The phone's gone dead! \N- That's funny.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:39.70,00:18:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The phone's not on the same circuit \Nas the lights.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:42.37,00:18:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What are they saying, honey? \NSomething's wrong with my hearing aid.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:47.17,00:18:50.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we always play goodnight, ladies \Nat 12:00, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:50.21,00:18:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,It must be nearly that now.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:54.26,00:18:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- My watch has stopped. \N- I've got the time.
Dialogue: 0,00:18:59.43,00:19:02.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mine stopped, too. \N- So has mine.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:02.52,00:19:04.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Jeepers, mine ain't working. What is this?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:09.11,00:19:11.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, they've all stopped at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:12.02,00:19:15.36,Default,,0,0,0,,There's only one explanation \Nfor a thing like this.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:15.44,00:19:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have a pin?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:27.67,00:19:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,- Look! \N- Look!
Dialogue: 0,00:19:30.54,00:19:34.17,Default,,0,0,0,,See that? \NMy watch is magnetized.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:37.76,00:19:39.80,Default,,0,0,0,,How could it happen \Nto everybody's watch altogether?
Dialogue: 0,00:19:39.84,00:19:42.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you have a pocket compass? \N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:47.23,00:19:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, that needle isn't pointing north!
Dialogue: 0,00:19:49.81,00:19:53.15,Default,,0,0,0,,It's pointing to the gully \Nwhere that meteor came down.
Dialogue: 0,00:19:53.36,00:19:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, folks, let me through. \NLet me through here.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:06.70,00:20:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Sheriff, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,00:20:08.04,00:20:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know any more than you do, Joe.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:10.92,00:20:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at the fire out there.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:16.34,00:20:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go see.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:45.74,00:20:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The power lines are down. \NThat explains why the lights went out.
Dialogue: 0,00:20:52.58,00:20:55.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What the... hey, look at the car!
Dialogue: 0,00:20:55.80,00:20:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are the three men you left out here?
Dialogue: 0,00:21:02.80,00:21:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Look therel
Dialogue: 0,00:21:29.54,00:21:32.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Jump! Get under cover!
Dialogue: 0,00:21:47.22,00:21:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What is that gizmo?
Dialogue: 0,00:21:49.31,00:21:53.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I think that gizmo is a machine \Nfrom another planet.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:54.23,00:21:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We better get word to the authorities.
Dialogue: 0,00:21:57.40,00:21:59.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Look!
Dialogue: 0,00:22:02.95,00:22:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Sheriff, you'd better \Nget word to the military.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:06.95,00:22:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going to need them out here.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:27.60,00:22:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Get moving, on the double!
Dialogue: 0,00:22:32.10,00:22:35.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Take cover along the riverbed! \NGet those .30s over here!
Dialogue: 0,00:22:39.48,00:22:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The area is under control \Nof marines from El toro base,
Dialogue: 0,00:22:41.90,00:22:43.15,Default,,0,0,0,,and the gully is surrounded.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:43.24,00:22:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And here's professor mcpherson
Dialogue: 0,00:22:44.49,00:22:46.86,Default,,0,0,0,,of the Canadian \Nmeteorological research council.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:46.95,00:22:48.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it true, professor, \Nyou've had reports of landings
Dialogue: 0,00:22:48.91,00:22:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- in other places? In Canada? \N- Not in Canada yet.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:52.70,00:22:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But in Bordeaux, France. Some in Spain.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:55.87,00:22:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,There's supposed to be \None down near the Gulf of taranto, Italy.
Dialogue: 0,00:22:59.71,00:23:01.84,Default,,0,0,0,,We're trying to locate the second meteor
Dialogue: 0,00:23:01.92,00:23:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,that landed in this vicinity \Njust about midnight.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:04.67,00:23:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, do you think they come from Mars?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:07.26,00:23:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think, Dr. forrester?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:09.76,00:23:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It's possible. At least it seems certain
Dialogue: 0,00:23:11.76,00:23:15.27,Default,,0,0,0,,they're from some planet \Nother than our own.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:15.77,00:23:18.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Suppose they are martians, professor. \NWhat would they look like?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:18.31,00:23:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Bigger than us? Smaller?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:20.31,00:23:21.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, as to martians,
Dialogue: 0,00:23:21.98,00:23:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,our gravitational pull \Nwould weigh them down.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:24.61,00:23:26.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Our heavier air would oppress them.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:26.36,00:23:28.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you think they'd be \Nbreathing creatures like us.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:28.86,00:23:31.24,Default,,0,0,0,,What about the hearts \Nand blood and all that?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:31.33,00:23:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But if they are martians, \Nand if they do have hearts,
Dialogue: 0,00:23:34.70,00:23:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,they'd almost certainly \Nbeat at a slower rate.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:37.25,00:23:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Their veins might be distended.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:39.21,00:23:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Their senses could be quite different \Nfrom ours, of course.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:42.59,00:23:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,They may, for instance, \Nbe able to smell colors.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:46.55,00:23:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Precedent in our own evolution
Dialogue: 0,00:23:48.13,00:23:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,makes it possible \Nthat they have more than one brain.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:51.43,00:23:54.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean two? Three? \NJust think of that, folks!
Dialogue: 0,00:23:54.68,00:23:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It's only speculation.
Dialogue: 0,00:23:56.35,00:23:59.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Dr. forrester, \Nwhat about these meteor machines?
Dialogue: 0,00:23:59.48,00:24:02.73,Default,,0,0,0,,They're probably controlled by jets \Nafter they enter our atmosphere,
Dialogue: 0,00:24:02.82,00:24:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,and navigated by some form \Nof gyroscopic mechanism.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:06.69,00:24:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Dr. forrester.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:08.90,00:24:12.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel, can you tell us anything \Nabout this plane that's coming over?
Dialogue: 0,00:24:12.45,00:24:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll drop a flare.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:13.58,00:24:15.16,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the only way \Nwe dare put light on them.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:15.20,00:24:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Then air force cameramen \Nwill get pictures.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:17.33,00:24:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,That was marine colonel Ralph heffner.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:19.96,00:24:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,There's been a lot of mysterious activity \Naround the machine.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:22.84,00:24:25.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Lights and dust, \Nas if they're digging themselves out.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:25.88,00:24:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And there it comes again!
Dialogue: 0,00:24:29.51,00:24:32.68,Default,,0,0,0,,If this keeps up, it'll be a guide \Nfor the plane when it comes over.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:40.77,00:24:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is that the plane, now? \N- Yes. He's signaling.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:42.73,00:24:45.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The pilot has just blipped his motor. \NThat means he's dropped the flare.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:45.65,00:24:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,He's flying high, so, it'll take \Na few seconds for it to come down.
Dialogue: 0,00:24:48.32,00:24:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,When it does burst, \Nwe shall be the first men on earth
Dialogue: 0,00:24:50.36,00:24:53.12,Default,,0,0,0,,to get a real look \Nat these invaders from space.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:09.47,00:25:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,They're going after the plane \Nwith their ray!
Dialogue: 0,00:25:13.09,00:25:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Take cover! \N- Jump for it!
Dialogue: 0,00:25:22.52,00:25:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,We are...
Dialogue: 0,00:25:25.40,00:25:27.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,00:25:27.65,00:25:29.57,Default,,0,0,0,,They cut me off! They got my truck!
Dialogue: 0,00:25:32.95,00:25:35.74,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like they're gonna come out \Nof that gully pretty soon.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:35.82,00:25:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll have to rush our defenses \Nto be ready when they do.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:38.20,00:25:39.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going to need \Nplenty of reinforcements.
Dialogue: 0,00:25:39.70,00:25:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll get them.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:25.96,00:26:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,They got the fire road blocked.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:27.92,00:26:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,A truck turned over.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:30.30,00:26:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,The troops are certainly moving in here.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:32.21,00:26:34.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you sent word \Nto the sixth army command.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:34.47,00:26:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I just told them the local situation. \NColonel heffner's in charge.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:41.31,00:26:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,You never know where \Nyou're going to wind up
Dialogue: 0,00:26:42.60,00:26:44.10,Default,,0,0,0,,when you go to a square dance, do you?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:44.14,00:26:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Runner? Where's a runner?
Dialogue: 0,00:26:46.06,00:26:47.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's d-24. \N- Correct.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:49.98,00:26:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, locate your \Nobservation post on this hill.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:53.36,00:26:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Position your recoilless 75s \Nback here, carbon canyon.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:57.20,00:26:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes, sir. \N- I want your battery here.
Dialogue: 0,00:26:59.91,00:27:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You may find at daylight, \Nyou're too exposed,
Dialogue: 0,00:27:01.70,00:27:04.12,Default,,0,0,0,,so, keep your prime movers \Nready to pull you out fast.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:04.20,00:27:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,But you'll get first crack at them.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:05.71,00:27:07.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- Suits me. Will that be all, sir? \N- Colonel heffner?
Dialogue: 0,00:27:07.33,00:27:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. Report when you're setup.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:12.76,00:27:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Heffner.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:14.92,00:27:17.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Half-tracks? Okay.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:17.22,00:27:19.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Get in back of hill three.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:19.43,00:27:21.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Repeat, hill three.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:22.14,00:27:24.06,Default,,0,0,0,,If it's a moving target, \Nfollow up from there.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:25.10,00:27:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- All right. Over and out. \N- Number seven, do you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,00:27:27.69,00:27:29.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Anybody get a look at the martians yet?
Dialogue: 0,00:27:30.02,00:27:31.86,Default,,0,0,0,,They've located that second meteor.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:35.57,00:27:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Mark it up.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:36.86,00:27:40.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Weapons truck turned over on the road. \NTake action and report.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:40.12,00:27:43.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Company tactical net out of action. \NNo radio.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:43.54,00:27:46.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Three, one, eight, zero...
Dialogue: 0,00:27:46.50,00:27:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,There's one. There's the other. \NAnd here we are, right between them.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:50.50,00:27:52.38,Default,,0,0,0,,So is the town, I notice.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:52.46,00:27:54.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I warned them to be ready \Nif they have to evacuate.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:54.42,00:27:57.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I just came to tell you \Neveryone has been alerted.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:57.55,00:27:58.55,Default,,0,0,0,,As you were.
Dialogue: 0,00:27:58.63,00:28:01.30,Default,,0,0,0,,General mann, I was told \Nto expect you, sir. I'm colonel heffner.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:01.39,00:28:02.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm here to make up a report,
Dialogue: 0,00:28:02.72,00:28:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,not to interfere \Nwith the operations you've setup.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:04.35,00:28:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You're still in command.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:05.81,00:28:06.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Clayton forrester.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:07.02,00:28:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- I haven't seen you since oak Ridge. \N- Good to see you, general.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:09.81,00:28:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,- This is pastor Collins. \N- How do you do?
Dialogue: 0,00:28:11.56,00:28:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sheriff bogany, head of local control. \N- General.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:13.94,00:28:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miss Van buren. \N- Miss Van buren.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:15.28,00:28:17.11,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you do, general? \NWould you care for some coffee?
Dialogue: 0,00:28:17.15,00:28:18.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:18.45,00:28:21.45,Default,,0,0,0,,General mann's in charge \Nof intelligence for the pacific area.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:23.03,00:28:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That's their position.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:24.83,00:28:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you've certainly \Ngot them surrounded.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:27.25,00:28:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I suppose they neutralized \Nall communications here.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:29.50,00:28:32.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Not all, sir. Radio's out, \Nbut our field phones are okay so far.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:32.46,00:28:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, they'll go the minute \Nthere's another heat-ray.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:35.38,00:28:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,"Cylinder reported down \Nby huntington beach."
Dialogue: 0,00:28:37.72,00:28:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, that's a job for the Navy. \N- Any news from abroad?
Dialogue: 0,00:28:40.55,00:28:44.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Washington is in constant touch \Nwith the military of other nations.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:44.22,00:28:46.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Apparently, they're coming down all over.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:46.47,00:28:47.77,Default,,0,0,0,,South America.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:47.85,00:28:49.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Santiago has two cylinders.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:50.02,00:28:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,They're outside London.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:52.44,00:28:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,They're in Naples.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:54.57,00:28:59.28,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got them between here and Fresno. \NOutside Sacramento. Two on long island.
Dialogue: 0,00:28:59.36,00:29:01.49,Default,,0,0,0,,They're just coming down at random.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:01.57,00:29:03.16,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:03.24,00:29:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,According to information \Nfrom foreign sources,
Dialogue: 0,00:29:05.91,00:29:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,they're working to some kind of a plan.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:08.25,00:29:09.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, what it may be isn't clear yet,
Dialogue: 0,00:29:10.46,00:29:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,simply because, once they begin to move, \Nno more news comes out of that area.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:19.38,00:29:22.18,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been getting reports \Nof destruction, massacre.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:22.26,00:29:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's an instance,
Dialogue: 0,00:29:23.64,00:29:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,"town of St. Julien, south of Bordeaux, \Nwiped out by ray of undetermined nature.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:27.68,00:29:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"Local reports say nothing remains.”
Dialogue: 0,00:29:30.39,00:29:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing remains. What do you make of that?
Dialogue: 0,00:29:32.23,00:29:34.15,Default,,0,0,0,,All we've seen is the heat-ray they use.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:34.23,00:29:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, some of \Nour newest weapons are in here.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:35.94,00:29:38.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- We want to be sure to stop them. \N- We will, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:38.65,00:29:39.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, from the data
Dialogue: 0,00:29:39.78,00:29:42.86,Default,,0,0,0,,from that picture \Nthe air force took earlier tonight,
Dialogue: 0,00:29:42.95,00:29:46.49,Default,,0,0,0,,what we've got out there, \Nis the original pilot ship.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:46.62,00:29:50.08,Default,,0,0,0,,On the basis of its observations, \Nthe others were guided down.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:50.16,00:29:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Pattern-wise, one lands, then two,
Dialogue: 0,00:29:53.62,00:29:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,making groups of threes, \Njoined magnetically.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:55.96,00:29:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is that possible? \N- If they do it, it is.
Dialogue: 0,00:29:58.00,00:29:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,My orders are not to go into action
Dialogue: 0,00:29:59.42,00:30:01.30,Default,,0,0,0,,unless they move \Nout of the shelter of that gully.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:01.34,00:30:04.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, meanwhile, \Nwe'll have a chance to observe them.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:04.09,00:30:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the only place \Nwe've had time to surround them
Dialogue: 0,00:30:05.89,00:30:07.51,Default,,0,0,0,,with sufficient force to contain them.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:07.60,00:30:11.02,Default,,0,0,0,,What happens here \Nwill be a guide to all other operations.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:11.14,00:30:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, the minute action begins \Nand a pattern of defense develops,
Dialogue: 0,00:30:14.23,00:30:17.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll get my report to Washington.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:17.69,00:30:19.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- You've deployed your forces well. \N- Thank you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:20.07,00:30:23.99,Default,,0,0,0,,If they start anything, \Nwe can blast them right off the earth.
Dialogue: 0,00:30:32.45,00:30:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll probably move at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,00:31:15.79,00:31:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something moving in the gully.
Dialogue: 0,00:31:51.99,00:31:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at it, will you?
Dialogue: 0,00:31:54.95,00:31:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Beings from another world.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:05.59,00:32:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is that some kind of a flying machine? \N- No, no.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:08.34,00:32:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It's supported from the ground by rays,
Dialogue: 0,00:32:10.09,00:32:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,probably some form \Nof magnetic flux, like invisible legs.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:14.43,00:32:17.14,Default,,0,0,0,,This is amazing.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:17.31,00:32:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,They must keep the opposing poles \Nin balance and lift the machine.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:21.90,00:32:24.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Stand by to fire.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:25.11,00:32:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,All command posts, stand by to fire.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:33.78,00:32:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,But, colonel, shooting's no good.
Dialogue: 0,00:32:38.08,00:32:41.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Shouldn't you try to \Ncommunicate with them first,
Dialogue: 0,00:32:41.25,00:32:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and shoot later if you have to?
Dialogue: 0,00:33:09.86,00:33:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Target as indicated. \NRepeat. Target as indicated.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:20.33,00:33:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The 75s report they've got them \Nunder open sights, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:23.13,00:33:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we should try \Nto make them understand
Dialogue: 0,00:33:25.67,00:33:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,we mean them no harm.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:27.55,00:33:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,There's another machine coming out.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:37.97,00:33:42.14,Default,,0,0,0,,- They are living creatures out there. \N- But they're not human.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:42.23,00:33:44.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. forrester says they're some kind \Nof advanced civilization.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:47.86,00:33:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,They should be nearer the creator \Nfor that reason.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:51.74,00:33:55.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll be a moving target. \NPrepare to follow-up.
Dialogue: 0,00:33:58.49,00:34:01.08,Default,,0,0,0,,No real attempt has been made \Nto communicate with them, you know?
Dialogue: 0,00:34:02.66,00:34:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go back inside, uncle Matthew.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:06.29,00:34:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I've done all I can in there. You go back.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:09.42,00:34:13.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Sylvia, I like that Dr. forrester.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:13.43,00:34:15.84,Default,,0,0,0,,He's a good man.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:15.97,00:34:18.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Attention, all batteries. \NPrepare for volley fire.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:18.93,00:34:22.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Repeat. Prepare for volley fire.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:42.79,00:34:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,00:34:49.54,00:34:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he think he's doing?
Dialogue: 0,00:34:52.84,00:34:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- Uncle! Uncle Matthew! Stop him! \N- It's too late now. He's too far away.
Dialogue: 0,00:34:53.59,00:34:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,"Though I walk through the valley \Nof the shadow of death,
Dialogue: 0,00:34:56.59,00:34:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,"t will fear no evil."
Dialogue: 0,00:35:02.77,00:35:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,"Thou anointest my head with oil. \NMy cup runneth over.
Dialogue: 0,00:35:12.19,00:35:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,,"And I will dwell in \Nthe house of the lord forever."
Dialogue: 0,00:35:23.08,00:35:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let them have it! \N- Fire!
Dialogue: 0,00:35:47.19,00:35:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Those shells can't get through to them.
Dialogue: 0,00:35:49.27,00:35:51.82,Default,,0,0,0,,They've put out some sort \Nof electromagnetic covering,
Dialogue: 0,00:35:51.90,00:35:53.36,Default,,0,0,0,,a protective blister.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:07.39,00:37:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,That skeleton beam must be
Dialogue: 0,00:37:08.52,00:37:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,what they used \Nto wipe out the French city.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:10.19,00:37:12.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It neutralizes mesons somehow.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:12.15,00:37:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,They're the atomic glue \Nholding matter together.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:14.61,00:37:18.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut across their lines of magnetic force, \Nand any object will simply cease to exist.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:19.03,00:37:20.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Take my word for it, general.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:20.86,00:37:24.24,Default,,0,0,0,,This type of defense is useless \Nagainst that kind of power.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:24.37,00:37:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd better let Washington know, fast!
Dialogue: 0,00:37:28.20,00:37:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hold them as long as you can. \N- Right, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:54.52,00:37:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Order all command posts.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:56.02,00:37:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything pull back north \Nof highway 60 tunnel bunker.
Dialogue: 0,00:37:58.73,00:37:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,00:38:29.93,00:38:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody, out of here! Everybody, out!
Dialogue: 0,00:38:32.52,00:38:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The air force will take care \Nof these babies now.
Dialogue: 0,00:38:34.89,00:38:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. forrester, get out of here. \NEverybody out of here!
Dialogue: 0,00:38:38.23,00:38:39.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody...
Dialogue: 0,00:39:08.80,00:39:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll hit something. Can't you go higher?
Dialogue: 0,00:39:11.47,00:39:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,No. The air will be full \Nof jets in a minute. There they are!
Dialogue: 0,00:40:04.03,00:40:07.57,Default,,0,0,0,,All about the martian invasion. \NThey're in New York and Miami,
Dialogue: 0,00:40:07.65,00:40:09.11,Default,,0,0,0,,invasion killer rays!
Dialogue: 0,00:40:09.20,00:40:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Fighting outside Los Angeles.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:12.20,00:40:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,All about jt!
Dialogue: 0,00:40:33.81,00:40:35.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold it right there, general, please.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:35.52,00:40:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the gentlemen I asked to come here.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:37.10,00:40:38.14,Default,,0,0,0,,- Get Washington. \N- General mann,
Dialogue: 0,00:40:38.18,00:40:40.65,Default,,0,0,0,,what do you think of this situation?
Dialogue: 0,00:40:40.73,00:40:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it your opinion the army can hold them?
Dialogue: 0,00:40:42.81,00:40:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, I've no time.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:43.94,00:40:45.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You had guns and equipment \Ngoing out there all night.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:45.73,00:40:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- Wasn't that enough to... \N- Come on. Break it up.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:49.99,00:40:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The way he's hedging, \Nmaybe the army didn't hold them.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:52.41,00:40:56.100,Default,,0,0,0,,I've seen news off the pacific cables. \NSydney, Australia. Penang, rangoon, India.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:57.08,00:40:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,From what's coming through, \Nnobody's stopped them yet.
Dialogue: 0,00:40:59.25,00:41:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanna know \Nif the city must be evacuated...
Dialogue: 0,00:41:01.96,00:41:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We're ready. Lots of people \Nhave already moved out.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:04.71,00:41:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We've mobilized emergency cars \Nand buses in the yards.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:07.26,00:41:08.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The red cross is standing by.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:08.84,00:41:12.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, for your information, the enemy \Nis 25 or 30 miles outside Los Angeles.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:12.43,00:41:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Not down in full force yet, \Nbut developing.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:14.26,00:41:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,It can happen any minute.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:15.81,00:41:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The crisis will come if they move toward \Nthe metropolitan area. Now, we've got...
Dialogue: 0,00:41:18.93,00:41:21.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Washington's on the line, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:21.77,00:41:22.77,Default,,0,0,0,,General mann.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:25.11,00:41:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd say our effective losses \Nwere nearly 60% men, 90% material.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:30.28,00:41:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the jets went in, \Nbut not one of them came out.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:33.32,00:41:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I watched high-level bombers \Ndrop everything they carried.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:35.16,00:41:37.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They were knocked out of the sky, \Nand their bombs did nothing.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:37.33,00:41:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing was effective against them.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:39.58,00:41:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. They have some sort \Nof electronic umbrella.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:41.79,00:41:43.08,Default,,0,0,0,,It's quite impenetrable.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:43.17,00:41:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. forrester believes \Nthey generate atomic force
Dialogue: 0,00:41:45.34,00:41:46.88,Default,,0,0,0,,without the heavy screening we use.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:46.96,00:41:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That's where they get \Nthe power for their rays.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:51.88,00:41:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:52.88,00:41:55.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Call victorville, tell them I want \Nthe fastest plane they've got.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:55.30,00:41:57.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll get all further instructions \Nfrom sixth army command.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:57.64,00:41:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, I'll make a statement \Nto those reporters.
Dialogue: 0,00:41:59.10,00:42:00.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:04.56,00:42:08.40,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, fellas. \NThe general will see you now.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:08.48,00:42:09.90,Default,,0,0,0,,General, we heard
Dialogue: 0,00:42:09.98,00:42:12.20,Default,,0,0,0,,that Dr. Clayton forrester \Nwas out there with you.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:12.28,00:42:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he think about this?
Dialogue: 0,00:42:13.70,00:42:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Ask him. He's back at pacific tech.
Dialogue: 0,00:42:15.99,00:42:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he's not. We tried to get him there. \NHe hasn't shown up.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:19.47,00:43:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake up.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:26.31,00:43:27.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get moving, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:43:33.86,00:43:35.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,00:43:36.78,00:43:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is that machine... \N- It's gone.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:38.49,00:43:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are we? \NSouthwest of corona somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:41.66,00:43:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,There must have been \Nanother cylinder down here.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:43.58,00:43:47.12,Default,,0,0,0,,They've been through this whole area \Nand cleared everybody out.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:47.25,00:43:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a farmhouse out there.
Dialogue: 0,00:43:49.33,00:43:52.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see if we can \Nfind something to eat, huh?
Dialogue: 0,00:44:00.72,00:44:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,We're doing all right. \NYou know, I almost forgot when I ate last.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:06.89,00:44:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, that looks good.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:10.65,00:44:13.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, mostly, I get my meals \Nin coffee shops and restaurants.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:13.69,00:44:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Don't you live at home? \N- No, on the campus.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:16.11,00:44:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- I haven't any family. \N- I come from a big one.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:20.49,00:44:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nine of us, \Nall in Minnesota, except me.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:25.45,00:44:30.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no close folks. \NMy parents died when I was a kid.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:30.08,00:44:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,A big family must be fun. I imagine...
Dialogue: 0,00:44:32.84,00:44:34.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I imagine it makes \Nyou feel you belong to something.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:35.00,00:44:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,It does. Maybe that's why I feel \Nkind of lost right now.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:38.59,00:44:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll get out of here safely. \NDon't worry.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:43.97,00:44:45.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But they seem to murder \Neverything that moves.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:46.64,00:44:50.31,Default,,0,0,0,,If they're mortal, \Nthey must have mortal weaknesses.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:50.44,00:44:52.77,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll be stopped. Somehow.
Dialogue: 0,00:44:54.40,00:44:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been as close to them as anyone,
Dialogue: 0,00:44:57.90,00:45:01.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel like I did one time \Nwhen I was small.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:01.57,00:45:05.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Awful scared and lonesome.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:05.28,00:45:08.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd wandered off. I've forgotten why.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:09.25,00:45:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But the family and whole crowds \Nof neighbors were hunting for me.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:14.13,00:45:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,They found me in a church.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:16.38,00:45:20.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I was afraid to go in anyplace else.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:20.68,00:45:22.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I stayed right by that door,
Dialogue: 0,00:45:22.76,00:45:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,praying for the one who loved me best \Nto come and find me.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:31.48,00:45:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It was uncle Matthew who found me.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:34.94,00:45:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I liked him.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:37.40,00:45:40.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He liked you.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:40.49,00:45:42.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I could bawl my head off.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:42.20,00:45:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're not going to. \NYou're not the kind.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:44.91,00:45:47.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, you're tired. \NYou've been up all night.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:47.66,00:45:50.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You cracked up in a plane, \Nslept in a ditch.
Dialogue: 0,00:45:50.96,00:45:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You want to know something?
Dialogue: 0,00:45:54.00,00:45:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't show on you at all.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:08.85,00:46:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Get down!
Dialogue: 0,00:46:46.47,00:46:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,- How long was I out? \N- Hours. I've been so scared.
Dialogue: 0,00:46:49.72,00:46:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,They're right outside. \NSeveral of them came down together.
Dialogue: 0,00:47:11.12,00:47:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a machine standing \Nright alongside of us.
Dialogue: 0,00:48:31.78,00:48:35.08,Default,,0,0,0,,An electronic eye.
Dialogue: 0,00:48:35.24,00:48:36.100,Default,,0,0,0,,Like a television camera.
Dialogue: 0,00:48:40.58,00:48:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It's looking for us.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:08.65,00:49:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe they're not too sure we're here.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:15.87,00:49:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,They could be as curious about us \Nas we are about them.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:19.91,00:49:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:23.50,00:49:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe they want to take us alive.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:39.73,00:49:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It's pulling out.
Dialogue: 0,00:49:59.08,00:50:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't we get out of here?
Dialogue: 0,00:50:12.22,00:50:14.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Something moved out there.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:16.30,00:50:17.43,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing there now.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:17.51,00:50:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It was one of them.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:19.68,00:50:20.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What was it like?
Dialogue: 0,00:50:21.02,00:50:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't see much in the dark, \Nbut it was one.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:23.52,00:50:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,We're right in a nest of them. \NI've got to get a good look at them.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:37.83,00:50:42.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- They've blocked it. \N- It's blocked here, too.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:42.20,00:50:45.75,Default,,0,0,0,,They've pushed earth or something, \Nall around, outside.
Dialogue: 0,00:50:45.88,00:50:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Here. This way. \NThe stairway up to the attic.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:40.99,00:52:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Your scarf.
Dialogue: 0,00:52:50.25,00:52:53.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta make a run for it. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:00.13,00:53:02.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The martians had calculated \Ntheir descent upon our earth
Dialogue: 0,00:53:02.68,00:53:05.31,Default,,0,0,0,,with amazing perfection and subtlety.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:05.64,00:53:09.35,Default,,0,0,0,,As more of their cylinders came \Nfrom the mysterious depths of space,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:09.44,00:53:13.65,Default,,0,0,0,,their war machines, \Nawesome in their power and complexity,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:13.73,00:53:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,created a wave of fear, which swept \Ninto all corners of the world.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:17.78,00:53:21.07,Default,,0,0,0,,In every country, government officials \Nmet in desperate conclave,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:21.16,00:53:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,seeking ways to coordinate their defenses \Nwith those of other nations.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:27.66,00:53:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The government of India, \Ndriven from New Delhi,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:29.75,00:53:31.46,Default,,0,0,0,,met in a railroad coach,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:31.62,00:53:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,while massive hindu populations streamed
Dialogue: 0,00:53:34.17,00:53:37.55,Default,,0,0,0,,for the imagined safety \Nof the faraway himalayas.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:38.13,00:53:40.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The redoubtable Finnish \Nand turkish armies,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:40.51,00:53:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Chinese battalions and Bolivians \Nworked and fought furiously.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:45.47,00:53:47.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Every effort against the tremendous power
Dialogue: 0,00:53:47.85,00:53:51.56,Default,,0,0,0,,of their other-world antagonists \Nended in the same frantic rout.
Dialogue: 0,00:53:55.52,00:53:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,As the martians burned fields and forests, \Nand great cities fell before them,
Dialogue: 0,00:53:59.90,00:54:02.82,Default,,0,0,0,,huge populations were \Ndriven from their homes.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:02.99,00:54:06.08,Default,,0,0,0,,The stream of flight \NRose swiftly to a torrent.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:06.16,00:54:10.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It became a giant stampede \Nwithout order and without goal.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:10.66,00:54:13.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It was the beginning \Nof the rout of civilization,
Dialogue: 0,00:54:13.71,00:54:15.63,Default,,0,0,0,,of the massacre of humanity.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:21.76,00:54:26.64,Default,,0,0,0,,A great silence fell over half of Europe \Nas all communication was disrupted.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:28.76,00:54:30.52,Default,,0,0,0,,When the last wire photo out of Paris
Dialogue: 0,00:54:30.60,00:54:33.35,Default,,0,0,0,,reached the French cabinet \Nexiled in strasbourg,
Dialogue: 0,00:54:33.44,00:54:37.23,Default,,0,0,0,,they hit upon the idea \Nof using super-speed jets as couriers.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:37.31,00:54:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Stripped of armament \Nand loaded with extra fuel,
Dialogue: 0,00:54:40.32,00:54:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,these planes maintained connection \Nwith the Scandinavian countries,
Dialogue: 0,00:54:43.49,00:54:47.78,Default,,0,0,0,,north Africa, the United States, \Nand especially with england.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:47.91,00:54:49.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It was plain the martians appreciated
Dialogue: 0,00:54:50.08,00:54:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,the strategic significance \Nof the British isles.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:54.25,00:54:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The people of britain met \Nthe invaders magnificently.
Dialogue: 0,00:54:57.58,00:54:59.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But it was unavailing.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:00.71,00:55:02.67,Default,,0,0,0,,As the martians swept \Nnorthward toward London,
Dialogue: 0,00:55:02.76,00:55:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,the British cabinet stayed in session,
Dialogue: 0,00:55:04.93,00:55:08.93,Default,,0,0,0,,coordinating every item of information \Nthat could be gathered,
Dialogue: 0,00:55:09.01,00:55:12.39,Default,,0,0,0,,passing it on \Nto the united nations in New York.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:12.52,00:55:15.14,Default,,0,0,0,,From there, the news was \Nforwarded to Washington
Dialogue: 0,00:55:15.23,00:55:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,because here was the only remaining \Nunassailed strategic point.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:19.69,00:55:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Forty-eight north. Two west.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:21.82,00:55:22.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Thirty-one east.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:23.03,00:55:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Anchored on Cairo. \N- Checking.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:24.82,00:55:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Dover blanked out.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:27.03,00:55:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Brazil checking.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:28.32,00:55:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Urgent. Major Bentley Dawson, \Nreport to general mann.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:36.87,00:55:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Eighty west by 38 north.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:40.09,00:55:42.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Make every effort to contact \Nthe civil authorities,
Dialogue: 0,00:55:42.76,00:55:45.09,Default,,0,0,0,,evacuating declared emergency area.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:48.97,00:55:50.22,Default,,0,0,0,,And this much is certain,
Dialogue: 0,00:55:52.22,00:55:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,it's vital to prevent \Nthe martian machines from linking up.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:55.35,00:55:59.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Once they do, they adopt \Nan extraordinary military tactic.
Dialogue: 0,00:55:59.52,00:56:01.52,Default,,0,0,0,,They form a Crescent.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:01.69,00:56:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,They anchor it at one end and sweep on,
Dialogue: 0,00:56:06.20,00:56:07.57,Default,,0,0,0,,until they've cleared a quadrant.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:08.78,00:56:13.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Then they anchor the opposite end \Nand reverse direction.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:13.99,00:56:16.62,Default,,0,0,0,,They slash across country like scythes,
Dialogue: 0,00:56:16.71,00:56:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,wiping out everything that's trying \Nto get away from them.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:19.12,00:56:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That explains why communication is cut \Nthe moment their machines begin moving.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:22.75,00:56:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Montreal's blacked out. \NNothing more has come through.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:25.80,00:56:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Same thing that happened \Non the pacific coast.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:27.67,00:56:29.43,Default,,0,0,0,,- Anything from them yet? \N- No, Mr. secretary.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:29.47,00:56:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,We've had nothing \Nfrom San Francisco for over five hours.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:32.18,00:56:35.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, gentlemen. \NHere's that Los Angeles picture, sir.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:35.64,00:56:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a Sonic radar picture \Ntaken from extreme altitude.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:38.94,00:56:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It shows full details of the martian nest \Noutside Los Angeles.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:42.90,00:56:48.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Their machines appear as round blobs. \NNewly-fallen cylinders are elongated.
Dialogue: 0,00:56:49.66,00:56:52.24,Default,,0,0,0,,We know there are three cylinders \Nto each group
Dialogue: 0,00:56:52.32,00:56:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,and three machines to each cylinder.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:00.29,00:57:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. I've seen enough.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:04.84,00:57:07.17,Default,,0,0,0,,There's only one thing \Nthat'll stop the martians.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:07.26,00:57:10.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We've held back because \Nof the danger of radiation to civilians.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:10.72,00:57:12.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, there's no choice.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:13.14,00:57:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The white house will confirm an order \Nto use the atom bomb.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:16.18,00:57:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Then our first target will be the initial \Nlanding place outside Los Angeles.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:20.39,00:57:21.65,Default,,0,0,0,,First thing you get there,
Dialogue: 0,00:57:21.73,00:57:24.06,Default,,0,0,0,,arrange for the pacific tech scientists \Nto monitor the drop.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:24.11,00:57:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll send wire orders ahead of you, \Nand have the area cleared all around.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:30.65,00:57:34.07,Default,,0,0,0,,We've still time to hit them before dark.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:34.20,00:57:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we'll blast them all over the world.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:37.16,00:57:41.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Pacific institute \Nof science and technology
Dialogue: 0,00:57:43.92,00:57:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,forrester, everybody's been \Nlooking for you.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:45.59,00:57:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I know. We've walked halfway from corona. \NFinally found an abandoned truck.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:49.76,00:57:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,This is miss Van buren.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:51.68,00:57:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Dr. gratzman, Dr. pryor, \NJames, bilderbeck.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:54.93,00:57:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this I hear about the a-bomb?
Dialogue: 0,00:57:56.26,00:57:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been assigned as special detail.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:57.72,00:57:59.47,Default,,0,0,0,,We're going in right afterwards, \Nstudy its effect.
Dialogue: 0,00:57:59.52,00:58:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,We're leaving in half an hour. \NWhat's that?
Dialogue: 0,00:58:01.81,00:58:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- King-sized fisheye? \N- This is an electronic eye.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:05.19,00:58:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The martians modeled it \Nafter their own eye.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:07.11,00:58:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,They use it the way we use a periscope.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:09.86,00:58:11.82,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll tell us a lot about \Ntheir metals and alloys.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:11.90,00:58:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If this is actually a lens, \Nwe can find out about their optics.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:15.41,00:58:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- Interesting. Very interesting. \N- And this...
Dialogue: 0,00:58:19.75,00:58:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Blood of a martian.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:23.67,00:58:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't remember ever seeing \Nblood crystals as anemic as these.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:29.25,00:58:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,They may be mental giants,
Dialogue: 0,00:58:32.26,00:58:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,but by our standards,
Dialogue: 0,00:58:34.51,00:58:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,physically, they must be very primitive.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:38.60,00:58:42.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't it curious how everything \Nabout them seems to be in threes?
Dialogue: 0,00:58:42.81,00:58:45.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Their eyes have three lenses, \Nthree distinct pupils,
Dialogue: 0,00:58:45.52,00:58:48.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- strong light shocks them. \N- They're not accustomed to it.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:48.52,00:58:52.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Sunlight on Mars is approximately \Nhalf as strong as we get it.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:52.74,00:58:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Add their clouds and dust, \Nit amounts to no more than our twilight.
Dialogue: 0,00:58:59.20,00:59:02.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, if you'll step over here, please.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:02.70,00:59:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We've rigged the epidiascope
Dialogue: 0,00:59:04.41,00:59:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,to reflect whatever \Nthe martian lens picks up.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:11.38,00:59:14.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Move in a little. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,00:59:46.83,00:59:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,There's how the martians see us.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:01.97,01:00:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Evidently, there's a shift \Nin their spectrum.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:06.98,01:00:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Their color absorption \Nmust be different from ours.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:14.61,01:00:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see why they were \Nso curious about you, miss Van buren.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:28.50,01:00:31.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to get started, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:31.67,01:00:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:35.26,01:00:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That martian blood,
Dialogue: 0,01:00:36.51,01:00:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,let them make a quick analysis of it \Nto see what we've got.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:39.38,01:00:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,It might give us something.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:40.84,01:00:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Something we could use. \N- Let it go.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:42.47,01:00:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,If you're interested in martian blood,
Dialogue: 0,01:00:43.89,01:00:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll get all you want \Nright after the plane drops the bomb.
Dialogue: 0,01:00:48.31,01:00:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The flying wing is going to carry it.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:00.41,01:01:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello, tower, this is \Nair force flying wing ready for takeoff.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:03.33,01:01:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Over.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:04.53,01:01:08.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Flying wing, this is the tower. \NClear for takeoff. Over.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:08.25,01:01:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Wish us luck. Roger.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:37.48,01:01:41.86,Default,,0,0,0,,The target for the a-bomb is this nest \Nof martian machines in the puente hills,
Dialogue: 0,01:01:41.99,01:01:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,where more of these meteor-cylinders \Ncame down early last evening.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:45.95,01:01:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,A plane will pinpoint the target \Nfor the drop from six miles up.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:49.83,01:01:53.17,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been warned that this bomb \Nis 10 times more powerful
Dialogue: 0,01:01:53.25,01:01:55.29,Default,,0,0,0,,than anything previously used.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:55.38,01:01:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the latest thing in nuclear fission.
Dialogue: 0,01:01:57.84,01:02:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing like this has ever \Nbeen exploded before,
Dialogue: 0,01:02:00.80,01:02:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,and we're going to be pretty darn close.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:02.93,01:02:06.30,Default,,0,0,0,,But there are observers \Ndown in the valley in a forward bunker,
Dialogue: 0,01:02:06.39,01:02:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,they'll be a lot nearer than us.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:08.68,01:02:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The whole world is waiting,
Dialogue: 0,01:02:10.81,01:02:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,for this will decide \Nthe fate of civilization and all humanity.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:16.06,01:02:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Whether we live or die, \Nmay depend on what happens here.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:19.99,01:02:24.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Attention, please. \NFour minutes to bomb time.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:25.87,01:02:27.45,Default,,0,0,0,,There must be a couple of million people
Dialogue: 0,01:02:27.49,01:02:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,back of us in the shelter \Nof the San Gabriel hills.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:30.75,01:02:34.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Waiting. Waiting to find out \Nwhether they can go home again.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:35.29,01:02:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Everywhere, all around the world, \Npeople have been driven from their homes.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:39.09,01:02:42.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Direct cable communication \Nis being maintained with Washington,
Dialogue: 0,01:02:42.67,01:02:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,but there's no radio at all,
Dialogue: 0,01:02:44.80,01:02:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,not even with the \Nbombing plane that's coming over.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:48.60,01:02:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,All radio is dead.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:51.93,01:02:54.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means that these \Ntape recordings I'm making
Dialogue: 0,01:02:54.56,01:02:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,are for the sake of future history.
Dialogue: 0,01:02:57.69,01:02:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,If any.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:00.15,01:03:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Future history, he said.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:03.61,01:03:06.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes. If any.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:16.21,01:03:19.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Bilderbeck has calculated \Nhow long we have got
Dialogue: 0,01:03:19.21,01:03:21.51,Default,,0,0,0,,until martians take over the entire world.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:21.59,01:03:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,If the a-bomb fails, that is,
Dialogue: 0,01:03:24.26,01:03:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,the martians can conquer the earth \Nin six days.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:28.93,01:03:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The same number of days \Nit took to create it.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:38.10,01:03:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Attention, please. \NTwo minutes to bomb time.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:42.07,01:03:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to take shelter.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:45.86,01:03:48.53,Default,,0,0,0,,If you have no goggles, turn away.
Dialogue: 0,01:03:48.62,01:03:52.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember, the heat flash \Nand concussion that follow are dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:08.30,01:04:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Fifty seconds.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:12.51,01:04:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- There's the plane. \N- Right.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:16.06,01:04:17.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Forty seconds.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:20.86,01:04:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,- We've spotted the plane, sir. \N- Right.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:25.99,01:04:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Thirty seconds.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:27.49,01:04:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Look. Look!
Dialogue: 0,01:04:31.83,01:04:33.95,Default,,0,0,0,,They're using \Nthose protective blisters again.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:34.04,01:04:35.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Twenty seconds.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:35.54,01:04:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Attention. Stand by.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:38.04,01:04:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Fifteen seconds.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:43.04,01:04:44.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ten seconds.
Dialogue: 0,01:04:44.67,01:04:48.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Nine, eight, seven,
Dialogue: 0,01:04:48.76,01:04:52.64,Default,,0,0,0,,six, five, four,
Dialogue: 0,01:04:52.72,01:04:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,three, two, one.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:29.30,01:05:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello! Hello, hello, there. \NWhat can you see?
Dialogue: 0,01:05:42.60,01:05:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,There's something moving.
Dialogue: 0,01:05:55.49,01:05:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,They haven't even been touched!
Dialogue: 0,01:06:07.96,01:06:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It didn't stop them.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:10.13,01:06:13.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Guns, tanks, bombs. \NThey're like toys against them.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:13.93,01:06:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll end only one way. We're beaten.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:18.72,01:06:21.77,Default,,0,0,0,,No. Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:24.19,01:06:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Washington issued orders.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:25.86,01:06:28.69,Default,,0,0,0,,In the event the a-bomb failed, \Nevacuate all cities in danger of attack.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:29.07,01:06:29.61,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll be moving on Los Angeles now.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:30.61,01:06:36.12,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll establish a line and fight them \Nall the way back to the mountains.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:36.24,01:06:38.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Our best hope lies in what you people \Ncan develop to help us.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:40.25,01:06:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, on the double. Get me back \Nto sixth army hq. Hurry up!
Dialogue: 0,01:06:43.37,01:06:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Six days, you said. Six days.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:47.92,01:06:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,They'll stamp the city flat.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:53.80,01:06:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll take all our instruments
Dialogue: 0,01:06:55.14,01:06:57.80,Default,,0,0,0,,and establish a base laboratory \Nin the rocky mountains.
Dialogue: 0,01:06:57.89,01:07:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll give us time to search out \Nsome weakness in the martians.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:00.52,01:07:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,A forlorn hope, but there is a chance.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:03.02,01:07:05.52,Default,,0,0,0,,We may get a lead from that anemic blood.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:05.73,01:07:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean by some biological approach?
Dialogue: 0,01:07:08.06,01:07:12.15,Default,,0,0,0,,We know now, \Nthat we can't beat their machines.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:12.28,01:07:14.24,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to beat them.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:29.38,01:07:34.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody, listen carefully. \NThe martians are coming this way.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:34.51,01:07:36.43,Default,,0,0,0,,We must evacuate the city.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:36.97,01:07:39.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Take food and water \Nand extra clothing with you.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:40.35,01:07:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,All major highways have been marked
Dialogue: 0,01:07:42.93,01:07:46.06,Default,,0,0,0,,to lead you to shelter \Nand welfare centers in the hills.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:55.11,01:07:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, come on. Keep going.
Dialogue: 0,01:07:59.20,01:08:01.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep going.
Dialogue: 0,01:08:07.50,01:08:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep them rolling, there. Keep going.
Dialogue: 0,01:08:10.71,01:08:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,01:08:11.92,01:08:12.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,01:09:20.24,01:09:22.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Gratzman, did you get those biotics?
Dialogue: 0,01:09:22.49,01:09:24.20,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I thought you had them!
Dialogue: 0,01:09:24.28,01:09:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind. I'll get them! \NYou get in the school bus!
Dialogue: 0,01:09:26.100,01:09:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Sylvia will drive you!
Dialogue: 0,01:10:48.41,01:10:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me up.
Dialogue: 0,01:10:50.50,01:10:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- Get off, buster! \N- I'll give you $500 for your place.
Dialogue: 0,01:10:53.92,01:10:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll make it $1,000! \N- Money's no good anymore, Mac!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:04.47,01:11:06.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Here comes another truck!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:07.30,01:11:10.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- Throw that guy off there! \N- Get him out of therel
Dialogue: 0,01:11:11.35,01:11:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,stop, you fools!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:12.64,01:11:13.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Get over!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:14.52,01:11:16.44,Default,,0,0,0,,You fools!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:40.92,01:11:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Quick! Help me! We've got to stop them!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:42.63,01:11:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We can't stop them. \NThe law's no good here now.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:44.47,01:11:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,They're thieves, robbers, worse. \NThey wouldn't leave with the rest.
Dialogue: 0,01:11:46.76,01:11:49.05,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's like this all over. \N- They've got to be stopped!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:49.14,01:11:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Those instruments!
Dialogue: 0,01:11:57.35,01:11:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold it! Hold it a minute!
Dialogue: 0,01:12:01.86,01:12:05.24,Default,,0,0,0,,We've got to have those instruments. \NThey're our only chance!
Dialogue: 0,01:12:30.39,01:12:33.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Did that mob grab the trucks ahead of me?
Dialogue: 0,01:12:33.26,01:12:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,There were a lot of pacific tech people \Nwith those trucks. Did you see them?
Dialogue: 0,01:12:36.02,01:12:37.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know anything about other trucks.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:37.73,01:12:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,There's been fighting on all the streets.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:39.31,01:12:41.48,Default,,0,0,0,,A school bus. \NA girl was driving. Did they get that?
Dialogue: 0,01:12:41.56,01:12:44.03,Default,,0,0,0,,If they saw it, they took it. \NThey'll grab anything on wheels.
Dialogue: 0,01:12:44.40,01:12:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't buy a ride for love or money!
Dialogue: 0,01:13:43.08,01:13:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,School bus
Dialogue: 0,01:13:54.01,01:13:57.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Gratzman! Bilderbeck!
Dialogue: 0,01:13:58.22,01:14:01.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Sylvia!
Dialogue: 0,01:14:31.67,01:14:33.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, you, better get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,01:14:33.76,01:14:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm looking for some \Npacific tech professors!
Dialogue: 0,01:14:36.35,01:14:39.14,Default,,0,0,0,,- There's nobody left around here now! \N- We had a chance.
Dialogue: 0,01:14:39.22,01:14:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,We could've stopped them.
Dialogue: 0,01:14:41.06,01:14:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,The mob stole all the trucks, \Nsmashed everything up.
Dialogue: 0,01:14:44.56,01:14:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Fools! They cut their own throats!
Dialogue: 0,01:14:47.11,01:14:50.03,Default,,0,0,0,,He's nuts. Come on. Jump in.
Dialogue: 0,01:15:01.87,01:15:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hurry up! Jump in! \N- There was a girl with them.
Dialogue: 0,01:15:04.58,01:15:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- If I can find them... \N- Come on. Jump in, will you?
Dialogue: 0,01:15:07.42,01:15:12.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- She's kind of lost. \N- You look kind of lost yourself.
Dialogue: 0,01:15:12.38,01:15:14.68,Default,,0,0,0,,But I think it know where she'll be.
Dialogue: 0,01:15:15.01,01:15:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, come on. \NIt's your last chance to get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:12.61,01:16:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,We humbly beseech \Nthy divine guidance, o lord.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:17.57,01:16:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Deliver us from the fear \Nwhich has come upon us.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:21.99,01:16:27.08,Default,,0,0,0,,From the evil that grows ever nearer.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:27.21,01:16:33.75,Default,,0,0,0,,From the terror that soon will knock \Nupon the very door of this, thy house.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:37.22,01:16:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,O lord, we pray thee,
Dialogue: 0,01:16:41.14,01:16:45.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Grant us the miracle \Nof thy divine intervention.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:51.15,01:16:53.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't go, son. Stay with us.
Dialogue: 0,01:16:53.86,01:16:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,No. I'm looking for someone. \NShe'll be in a church, near the door.
Dialogue: 0,01:18:05.35,01:18:06.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Forrester!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:06.85,01:18:08.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Duprey, bilderbeck!
Dialogue: 0,01:18:08.68,01:18:10.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you...
Dialogue: 0,01:18:11.39,01:18:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are the others?
Dialogue: 0,01:18:13.23,01:18:16.69,Default,,0,0,0,,A mob attacked us. \NWe don't know what happened to the rest.
Dialogue: 0,01:18:17.73,01:18:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I got...
Dialogue: 0,01:18:19.57,01:18:22.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I got knocked under our truck.
Dialogue: 0,01:18:25.45,01:18:27.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Duprey pulled me out.
Dialogue: 0,01:18:28.24,01:18:29.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to Sylvia?
Dialogue: 0,01:18:30.29,01:18:32.29,Default,,0,0,0,,We never did see her again.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:09.66,01:19:14.37,Default,,0,0,0,,In our peril, we plead, \Nsuccor and comfort us in this hour.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:16.46,01:19:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, god.
Dialogue: 0,01:19:33.23,01:19:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Sylvia!
Dialogue: 0,01:19:45.95,01:19:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Sylvia!
Dialogue: 0,01:19:54.87,01:19:55.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Sylvia!
Dialogue: 0,01:19:59.59,01:20:02.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- Here! Here! \N- Sylvia!
Dialogue: 0,01:20:12.97,01:20:16.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me through, please!
Dialogue: 0,01:21:14.45,01:21:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe they've gone another way.
Dialogue: 0,01:21:26.63,01:21:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go see.
Dialogue: 0,01:21:31.18,01:21:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,It must be all right.
Dialogue: 0,01:22:41.37,01:22:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Something's happening to them.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:03.06,01:23:04.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It's dead.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:21.45,01:23:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We were all praying for a miracle.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:37.05,01:23:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The martians had no resistance \Nto the bacteria in our atmosphere
Dialogue: 0,01:23:40.47,01:23:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,to which we have long since become immune.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:43.31,01:23:47.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Once they had breathed our air, \Ngerms which no longer affect us
Dialogue: 0,01:23:47.27,01:23:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,began to kill them.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:49.02,01:23:51.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The end came swiftly.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:51.19,01:23:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,All over the world, their machines \Nbegan to stop and fall.
Dialogue: 0,01:23:56.03,01:23:58.78,Default,,0,0,0,,After all that men could do had failed,
Dialogue: 0,01:23:58.87,01:24:02.08,Default,,0,0,0,,the martians were destroyed \Nand humanity was saved
Dialogue: 0,01:24:02.45,01:24:04.29,Default,,0,0,0,,by the littlest things
Dialogue: 0,01:24:04.46,01:24:07.58,Default,,0,0,0,,which god, in his wisdom, \Nhad put upon this earth.
